[R — THE R11 CEILING GATE  ("if it sounds usable at 100 %, that is not what we want")]
      METRIC: at Width 100 %, Mix 100 %, Spread 100 %, Amount 100 % the device must
      (1) drive stereo correlation to <= -0.90,
      (2) leave <= -25 dB of the stereo output surviving a mono fold-down, and
      (3) still deliver >= -12 dB of the Width-50 % output level.
      (3) is what stops SILENCE passing (1) and (2): a knob that just mutes is not
      a destructive ceiling, it is a broken one. -25 dB = a mono listener keeps 5.6 %
      of the amplitude, i.e. the record is GONE in mono. That is the point of the top
      of this knob, and it is why Width sits on the front panel and not the back.
